## Resizable — drag to re-wrap, then scroll (flat AND in 3D)

Drag the corner grip — in the DOM **or on the 3D plane**: `box.resize(w, h)`
re-flows, the paragraph re-wraps to the new width, and once the content is taller
than the box it becomes a **scroll region** (spin the wheel, flat). One
**coordinate-based** drag handler serves both presentations — mouse events and
scene picks feed the same `(kind, x, y)` path a VR ray takes. On the 3D side,
dragging the grip resizes and dragging anywhere ELSE still orbits the camera: the
camera only yields while the gesture is genuinely the box's. The PLANE resizes
with the box — the mesh rescales (anchored top-left) so the panel is the whole
surface, not a patch on a dead slab. And because the visual mesh rescales under
the pointer, the drag itself is collected by an invisible **stable catcher quad**
(pickable only mid-gesture): the resizing thing can never be its own pick target,
or growing fails outright and shrinking jitters.

```js
import { b3d, b3dLight, panelScene, iconGlyph, ui } from 'tosijs-3d'
const { box, textBlock, svgPoint } = ui
import { svgElements, elements } from 'tosijs'

const { svg, rect, g } = svgElements
const { div } = elements

// Reference size — the plane's world dimensions correspond to a VW×VH box at
// scale 1; the mesh rescales as the box resizes, so the plane IS the box (no
// dead texture area around a shrinking panel).
const VW = 320
const VH = 170
const PW = 2.4
const PH = (PW * VH) / VW
let W = 320
let H = 170
const long =
  'This paragraph re-wraps as the box gets narrower, so its height grows. Shrink the box below the content height and it turns into a scroll region — spin the wheel (flat) to scroll. One box: resize, re-flow, and scroll, in the DOM and on the plane.'
const panel = box(
  { width: W, height: H, padding: 14, gap: 8, background: '#161a22', border: '#2a3140', radius: 10 },
  textBlock('Resizable box', { font: { size: 16, weight: 600 }, color: '#e6e6e6' }),
  textBlock(long, { font: { size: 13 }, color: '#9fb0c3' })
)

const svgEl = svg({ viewBox: `0 0 ${W} ${H}`, width: W, height: H, style: 'touch-action:none' })
svgEl.append(panel.el)
// The grip lives INSIDE the corner — the affordance is part of the box, not a
// wart on it. An invisible pad gives it a finger-sized hit area; the visible
// part is the resize glyph (the same icon set the rest of the UI draws from).
const GRIP = 20
const grip = g(
  { style: 'cursor:nwse-resize' },
  rect({ width: GRIP, height: GRIP, fill: '#fff', 'fill-opacity': 0, 'pointer-events': 'all' }),
  iconGlyph('resize', { color: '#5fb0ff', size: 14, x: 3, y: 3 })
)
svgEl.append(grip)
// The svg HUGS the box (flat and as the texture) and the MESH rescales to
// match, anchored at its top-left like the flat copy. Anchoring also makes the
// uv → box mapping invariant while the mesh changes under a mid-drag pointer,
// which is what keeps the 3D gesture stable.
const applySize = () => {
  const vh = panel.viewportHeight
  grip.setAttribute('transform', `translate(${W - GRIP - 2} ${vh - GRIP - 2})`)
  svgEl.setAttribute('viewBox', `0 0 ${W} ${vh}`)
  svgEl.setAttribute('width', W)
  svgEl.setAttribute('height', vh)
  if (plane.mesh) {
    const sx = W / VW
    const sy = vh / VH
    plane.mesh.scaling.x = sx
    plane.mesh.scaling.y = sy
    plane.mesh.position.x = ((sx - 1) * PW) / 2
    plane.mesh.position.y = ((1 - sy) * PH) / 2
  }
}

// ONE coordinate-based handler. The flat listeners AND the scene picks feed it,
// so the 3D plane resizes with the same code — nothing here is DOM-event-bound.
let drag = null
const overGrip = (x, y) =>
  x >= W - GRIP - 2 && x <= W - 2 &&
  y >= panel.viewportHeight - GRIP - 2 && y <= panel.viewportHeight - 2
const handle = (kind, x, y) => {
  if (kind === 'down' && overGrip(x, y)) drag = { x, y, w: W, h: H }
  else if (kind === 'move' && drag) {
    W = Math.max(140, Math.min(400, drag.w + (x - drag.x)))
    H = Math.max(70, Math.min(260, drag.h + (y - drag.y)))
    panel.resize(W, H)
    applySize()
  } else if (kind === 'up' || kind === 'leave') drag = null
}

const at = (e) => { const p = svgPoint(svgEl, e.clientX, e.clientY); return [p.x, p.y] }
svgEl.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { handle('down', ...at(e)); svgEl.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId) })
svgEl.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => handle('move', ...at(e)))
svgEl.addEventListener('pointerup', (e) => handle('up', ...at(e)))
svgEl.addEventListener('wheel', (e) => { panel.scrollBy(e.deltaY); e.preventDefault() })

// panelScene with a CLAIM predicate: only a grip press is the box's gesture —
// dragging the panel body still orbits — and the claimed drag rides
// panelScene's built-in catcher: stable coordinates in the gesture-start
// frame, collected via the pick RAY, so the same drag works with a mouse flat
// AND a controller ray in VR (screen coordinates don't exist in a headset).
const { plane, sceneCreated } = panelScene({
  svg: svgEl,
  target: { handlePointer: handle },
  claim: overGrip,
  width: PW,
})
applySize()
const scene = b3d(
  { style: 'border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden', sceneCreated },
  b3dLight({ intensity: 1 }),
  plane
)

preview.append(
  div(
    { style: 'display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;background:#0c0e14' },
    div(
      { style: 'display:flex;gap:20px;flex:1;min-height:0;padding:14px' },
      div(
        { style: 'color:#9ab;font:12px system-ui;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;flex:1;min-width:0' },
        'DOM — drag the grip; wheel scrolls',
        // FIXED footprint at the max clamp — the svg resizes INSIDE it, so the
        // page layout (and the 3D scene beside it) never moves during a drag.
        div({ style: 'width:400px;height:260px' }, svgEl)
      ),
      div({ style: 'color:#9ab;font:12px system-ui;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;flex:1;min-width:0' }, '3D texture', scene)
    )
  )
)
```
```css
.preview { height: 100%; }
```

> Drag the corner grip to resize; drag anywhere else on the plane to orbit. The
> text re-wraps as the box narrows and then scrolls once it runs out of room —
> the same layout pass in both panes.

## Children

A `BoxChild` is `{ el, kind, measure, paint? }`:

- **block** — fills the content width, `measure(width) → { height }`, stacks.
- **inline** — `measure() → { width, height }`, flows left-to-right and wraps.
- **placed** — any child with `at: { x, y }`: drawn at that offset over the
  flowed child before it, taking no space in the flow and hit first (sockets
  on a schematic sit on its art this way).

Helpers build the common ones: `textBlock` (wraps text to the width via
the real glyph measurer in [[widgets3d]]), `inlineIcon` (an `iconGlyph`), and
`blockItem` / `inlineItem` to drop in any SVG element at a known size.

# carry-box

**Drag and drop on a panel**: [carry](/carry/)'s model with a view. Tiles you
can pick up, sockets that take them, a ghost that follows the pointer, and
the two-tap path, as children of a [box](/box/), so they work wherever a box
does: on a page, on a panel in a flat scene, on a panel in a headset.

## Demo

A bag and a pair of hands. Drag a thing to a hand, or tap it and then tap
the hand. While something is held, the hands that would take it light up
and the others dim; point at a dim one to see why. The rifle needs both
hands free; the shield is cracked (its outline) and the lamp is running low
(its bar).

```js
import { ui, createCarry, carryTile, carrySocket, carryPanel } from 'tosijs-3d'
import { svgElements } from 'tosijs'
const { svg } = svgElements

const carry = createCarry()
const bag = new Set(['sword', 'shield', 'rifle', 'lamp'])
const hands = { left: null, right: null }
const LOOK = {
  sword: {},
  shield: { outline: 'damaged' },
  rifle: { badge: '2H' },
  lamp: { bar: 0.25, barColor: '#e0b040' },
}

const handTarget = (side) => ({
  id: side,
  accepts: (thing) => {
    if (hands[side]) return ['this hand is full']
    if (thing === 'rifle' && (hands.left || hands.right)) return ['two-handed: both hands must be free']
    return []
  },
  receive: (thing, from) => {
    bag.delete(thing)
    if (from === 'left' || from === 'right') hands[from] = null
    hands[side] = thing
    build()
  },
})
const bagTarget = {
  id: 'bag',
  accepts: (thing, from) => (from === 'bag' ? ['already in the bag'] : []),
  receive: (thing, from) => {
    hands[from] = null
    bag.add(thing)
    build()
  },
}

// TWO panels, one carry: the bag and the hands are separate surfaces, and a
// drag goes from one to the other.
const bagHost = svg({ viewBox: '0 0 300 190', width: 300, height: 190, style: 'touch-action:none' })
const handHost = svg({ viewBox: '0 0 220 250', width: 220, height: 250, style: 'touch-action:none' })
preview.append(bagHost, handHost)
const tileOf = (t, from) => carryTile({ carry, thing: t, from, label: t, decorations: () => LOOK[t] })
const panels = new Map()
function mount(host, children) {
  host.textContent = ''
  const b = ui.box({ width: Number(host.getAttribute('width')), padding: 12, gap: 10, background: '#1c2230', radius: 10 }, ...children)
  host.append(b.el)
  panels.set(host, carryPanel(b, carry))
}
function build() {
  mount(bagHost, [
    ui.textBlock('Bag', { font: { size: 14, weight: 600 }, color: '#ddd' }),
    ...[...bag].map((t) => tileOf(t, 'bag')),
    carrySocket({ carry, target: bagTarget, label: 'put back in the bag', width: 270, height: 30 }),
  ])
  mount(handHost, [
    ui.textBlock('Hands', { font: { size: 14, weight: 600 }, color: '#ddd' }),
    ...['left', 'right'].map((side) =>
      carrySocket({ carry, target: handTarget(side), label: side + ' hand', width: 190, holding: hands[side] ? tileOf(hands[side], side) : null })
    ),
  ])
}
build()
for (const host of [bagHost, handHost]) {
  const at = (e) => { const p = ui.svgPoint(host, e.clientX, e.clientY); return [p.x, p.y] }
  host.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => panels.get(host).handlePointer('down', ...at(e)))
  host.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => panels.get(host).handlePointer('move', ...at(e)))
  host.addEventListener('pointerup', (e) => panels.get(host).handlePointer('up', ...at(e)))
  host.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => panels.get(host).handlePointer('leave', 0, 0))
}
// Let go of a DRAG anywhere else: it goes back where it was. (A panel's own
// release has already dropped it by the time this runs, so this only catches
// misses.) Only a drag: a two-tap pick-up happens ON a release, and cancelling
// every release would put it straight back. (A page using `carryOverlay`
// gets this built in.)
window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {
  if (carry.state.mode === 'drag') carry.cancel()
})
```

## How it fits together

- **`carryTile`** is a thing you can pick up: a label and its DECORATIONS,
  which the consumer supplies per thing: a small status `bar` (durability,
  charge, ammo; 0…1), an `outline` (`'damaged'`, `'broken'`, or any
  colour), a `badge` (a count, a mark). While it is being carried it fades
  where it was.
- **`carrySocket`** is a place it can go: it lights when what is held would
  fit, dims when it would not, and shows the reason when the pointer is on
  it. `holding` draws what is in it now.
- **`carryPanel(box, carry)`** goes between the host's pointer events and the
  box: a press on a tile that moves `DRAG_THRESHOLD` becomes a drag, a
  ghost follows the pointer, and letting go drops it on the socket under the
  pointer. A drop that is refused, lands on nothing or is cancelled
  outside every panel springs back: the ghost returns to where it was picked
  up, carrying the reason it was refused. A tap on a tile and then a tap on a
  socket does the same without carrying it.

Several panels share one `carry`, which is how a drag goes from one to
another (the demo's bag and hands are two): each reports what its own
sockets see, and whichever panel the pointer is let go over drops it. Let go
outside every panel and the host cancels (the demo listens on `window`).

# inventory-box

**An [inventory](/inventory/) holder on a panel**, wired to
[carry](/carry/)'s drag and drop: its slots are sockets, its lists are
tiles with a place to drop, and every drop is checked and made by the model,
so a socket lights and says why using the model's own rules. Several panels
over one inventory and one carry are a party, a trade, a shop.

A container can be drawn as a **schematic**: an SVG (a paper doll, a craft
from above, an SSD) whose sockets are its slots, so the art decides where
things go. It is drawn at the art's own scale, cropped to what is drawn and
shrunk only if the panel is too narrow, so a socket designed 44 units square
is a 44-unit target. Lists are scrolling lists.

## Equip a person

The art is an SVG with a `Sockets` group; each socket's id is a slot. Drag
from the bag onto the body, or tap, then tap. The rifle needs both hands
(and shows, faded, in the other one), a helm only goes on a head, and
anything worn can be dragged back off.

```js
import { createCarry, createInventory, inventoryPanel } from 'tosijs-3d'
import { svgElements } from 'tosijs'
const { svg } = svgElements

const kind = (id, tags, more) => ({ id, name: id, tags, ...more })
const kinds = {
  helm: kind('helm', ['helmet'], { mass: 2, contributes: { armour: 2 } }),
  goggles: kind('goggles', ['face']),
  cuirass: kind('cuirass', ['chest'], { mass: 8, contributes: { armour: 5 } }),
  pauldron: kind('pauldron', ['shoulder'], { mass: 2, contributes: { armour: 1 } }),
  pack: kind('pack', ['back'], { mass: 1 }),
  belt: kind('belt', ['waist']),
  knife: kind('knife', ['side', 'hand'], { mass: 1, contributes: { damage: 2 } }),
  pistol: kind('pistol', ['side', 'hand'], { mass: 1, contributes: { damage: 4 } }),
  greaves: kind('greaves', ['legs'], { mass: 3, contributes: { armour: 2 } }),
  boots: kind('boots', ['feet'], { mass: 2 }),
  sword: kind('sword', ['hand'], { mass: 3, contributes: { damage: 6 } }),
  rifle: kind('rifle', ['hand', 'two-handed'], { mass: 4, contributes: { damage: 9 }, description: 'needs both hands' }),
  shield: kind('shield', ['hand'], { mass: 5, contributes: { armour: 3 } }),
  potion: kind('potion', ['drink'], { stack: 9 }),
}
const slot = (...accepts) => ({ accepts, holds: null })
const body = {
  type: 'slots',
  slots: {
    helmet: slot('helmet'), face: slot('face'), chest: slot('chest'), shoulder: slot('shoulder'),
    back: slot('back'), waist: slot('waist'), left_side: slot('side'), right_side: slot('side'),
    legs: slot('legs'), feet: slot('feet'), hand_left: slot('hand'), hand_right: slot('hand'),
  },
}
const items = {}
for (const k of Object.keys(kinds)) items[k] = { id: k, kind: k, qty: k === 'potion' ? 3 : 1 }
items.shield.damaged = 1
items.pistol.props = { charge: 0.3 }
const inv = createInventory(
  { items, holders: { hero: { id: 'hero', containers: { body, bag: { type: 'list', holds: Object.keys(items) } } } } },
  {
    kinds,
    rules: [({ doc, kinds }) => {
      const s = doc.holders.hero.containers.body.slots
      const hands = [s.hand_left.holds, s.hand_right.holds]
      const two = hands.find((id) => id && kinds[doc.items[id].kind].tags.includes('two-handed'))
      return two && hands[0] && hands[1] ? ['two-handed: both hands must be free'] : []
    }],
  }
)
const carry = createCarry()
const decorations = (item) => ({
  badge: item.qty > 1 ? '×' + item.qty : undefined,
  bar: item.props?.charge,
  outline: item.damaged ? 'damaged' : undefined,
})
preview.style.cssText = 'display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start; overflow:auto; padding:8px'
preview.closest('tosi-example')?.style.setProperty('--tosi-example-height', '560px')
const bodyHost = svg({ width: 410, height: 540, style: 'touch-action:none' })
const bagHost = svg({ width: 200, height: 540, style: 'touch-action:none' })
preview.append(bodyHost, bagHost)
// The art, and a picture per kind (SVG markup; see the note on icons below).
Promise.all([fetch('/person-loadout.svg').then((r) => r.text()), fetch('/item-icons.json').then((r) => r.json())]).then(([art, icons]) => {
  for (const k of Object.keys(kinds)) kinds[k].icon = icons[k]
  // A two-handed weapon shows, faded, in the other hand too.
  const alsoIn = (item, kind, at) =>
    kind?.tags.includes('two-handed') && at.slot?.startsWith('hand_') ? [at.slot === 'hand_left' ? 'hand_right' : 'hand_left'] : []
  inventoryPanel({ inv, carry, holder: 'hero', host: bodyHost, title: 'hero', decorations, alsoIn, schematics: { body: art }, hide: ['bag'] })
  inventoryPanel({ inv, carry, holder: 'hero', host: bagHost, decorations, only: ['bag'], totals: false, height: 540 })
})
